=== 1. unquoted body: backslash escapes only $ ` \ and newline
\"quoted\" \'single\' \a \n \t
$v `echo no` \ val
joined line
=== 2. generated JSON / C keeps its escaped quotes
{"name": "val", "text": "say \"hi\""}
printf("%s\n", "\"val\"");
=== 3. <<- strips tabs, escapes unchanged
\"tab\" $v
=== 4. quoted delimiter: body verbatim
\" \$v \\ \
=== 5. heredoc inside command substitution
\"in subst\" $v
=== 6. double quotes still escape " (unchanged)
a"b " "
